  (text "PAL dumper shield (PALDump by Dmitry Shtatnov, github.com/rpocc/PALDump). One 24-pin ZIF socket:\n20-pin PALs (PAL10L8, PAL16L8) flush with pin 1, S2 on \"20\"; 24-pin PALs (PAL20L8) S2 on \"24\".\nS1 off = PAL unpowered and Arduino held in reset; S1 on = dump starts. Every contact has a 270R series resistor,\ncontacts 15-23 can carry PAL outputs and get a 1k to the probe line (tri-state detection).\ngithub.com/sfambach/PALDump - fambach.net - hardware CERN-OHL-S-2.0"
    (at 76.2 265 0)
    (effects
      (font
        (size 1.27 1.27))
      (justify left))
    (uuid "e211e569-703d-452b-ad89-be53733ac71c"))
